    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` feature following the established derived-flag pattern (mirroring `capacityWarning`/`possibleDuplicate`). `riskFlag` is `true` when **any** of the three signals holds, else `false`:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 reads `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()`, set by the prior `possibleDuplicate` step.\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 a near-variant of a blocklisted disposable domain that dodges the exact-match rejection (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `x.mailinator.com`), matched by second-level domain label.\n3. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 the city holds \u2265 40 owners (the soft threshold `WARN_LOW`, below the hard cap of 50).\n\n### Changes\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean riskFlag` field with getter/setter (never persisted).\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean property so it's generated into `OwnerDto` and mapped implicitly by MapStruct (name match).\n- **`rest/function/owner/OwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 added package-private `isDisposableAdjacent(email)` (plus a `secondLevelLabel` helper), keeping disposable-domain knowledge in one place alongside the existing blocklist.\n- **`rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerRiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 the step that composes the three signals and sets the flag.\n- **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** and **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignRiskFlag` step after `possibleDuplicate` (before `respond`), under the pipeline's `transaction` / `readonly-transaction` governance, so create and GET responses compute the same value.\n\nThe one existing/new test, `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`, passes: a lone `structuredOwner()` (no email, unique fields, city count 1) yields `riskFlag: false`.",
